MAJOR_VERSION=5
STANDARD_VERSION=3
RELEASE_VERSION=0
PRERELEASE=1
DEV_VERSION=11
DESCRIPTION=Six story slices. FL-22: the kernel workqueue grows delayed and periodic work (fl_wq_enqueue_at, fl_wq_enqueue_every, fl_wq_poll_at) held in a small time-ordered timer array and moved into the MLQ when due, FL_WQ_PROTECTED items that use a reserve of slots and run once at shutdown instead of being discarded, a nested-poll guard per queue instead of one global counter, and a per-queue mutex on hosted builds; the shell now starts a ticker thread (fl_bg_jobs_ticker_start) that is the only poller of the default queue, so fl_bg_jobs_tick is driven for the first time. The duplicate priority queue copies (repository root and src/) are deleted and the build uses kernel/core/sched/priority_queue.c. The browser image compiles the same queue sources (-DFL_FREESTANDING: no lock, a static item pool) and drives them from the PIT tick. Durable work (FL-25): fl_wq_enqueue_durable journals a job before accepting it, stages a bounded window into the queue, runs registered handlers by tag with retries, recovers at boot (cut-off work retried, stale work expired unrun, user-visible work held for its owner), and refuses with BUSY when the journal is full; the journal is an installable table, memory only by default and in the image, with a flushed SQLite backend for the hosted build. FL-17: CI now runs test_kq_checkpoint, test_kq_delivery, test_kq_net and test_kq_wire, and test_heritage pins that a 31-character account name is accepted, and test_freestanding_shell.py runs one scripted account session on the lab image and on the hosted shell and compares them. FL-04 (partial): session wire opcodes KQH_REQ 0x50 and KQH_DATA 0x51 in a second KeyQuorum range routed to the existing KeyQuorum hook, with invariant tests, and the history bundle framing (kernel/core/vfs/kq_history_bundle.[ch], two length-prefixed KQPB letters) with its own test; the host and client handlers are not built and a 0x50 or 0x51 frame is dropped until they are. FL-02 stage 1 (needs the KeyQuorum pin at 8ab454b, a commit on KeyQuorum's open pull request): the browser image links the KeyQuorum library built for x86_64-unknown-none and the existing driver (kq_platform.c: heap arena, RDRAND entropy that fails closed, CMOS UTC clock, the libc symbols the archive needs), prints CAP keyquorum=linked after the ABI probe, and the build refuses an image whose bss reaches the end of conventional memory; the delivery checkpoints are not in the image. FL-04 handlers: the host answers KQH_REQ through a gate and a source it is given (refusing visibly when either is missing), the client reassembles KQH_DATA into the two letters, with driver ops for the kind-17 snapshot and KQER error reports and the authz op codes 11 to 18 appended. FL-17 item 3: the bridge-reach assertion over kq_bridge_connects. FL-15 part A: the account store gains auth_mode, the account_keys / account_bridges / account_assembly tables and the KQST path accessor; the login hand-off to the key service is not built.

RELEASE_DATE=2026-11-03
